What is the name of the file that defaced the imreallynotbatman.com website? Please submit only the name of the file with extension?
I now pivoted to look for POST requests sent to the website. If an attacker is going to deface a website, they will likely need to upload their malicious document. I had to research how exactly to form this query, but this is what I ended up running:
"imreallynotbatman.com" src_ip=40.80.148.42 "POST" url IN ("*jpg, *doc*)
This gave 29 results, so my first attempt was to check the first result given: win.ini.jpg
That was incorrect, so I analyzed the logs further. After looking at the statics for URLs, I noticed that's the only one in these results. From there, I pivoted to get rid of the POST filter. Perhaps it will show the information of them pulling the information instead of when they posted it. I saw a URL then of imnotbatman.jpg, which seemed promising, but unfortunately, was still not the correct answer. Then, I figured, if the request would be pulling from the site, then the DESTINATION IP would be what I filter the given IP on. Next, I found some_inexistent_file_with_long_name_00.jpg, but alas, still not correct. I kept getting a more and more complex query because I was trying to search FOR "jpg" and "doc" BUT NOT the strings we've already confirmed to be incorrect.
Finally, I decided to wait just a couple minutes for the hint to become available. It said, "First find the IP address of the web server hosting imreallynotbatman.com." So, I found the imreallynotbatman.com has the IP of 192.168.250.70.
My new query was: src_ip=192.168.250.70 dest_ip=40.80.148.42 filename="*jpg"
I did this with the intent to iterate through common filetypes. That also returned nothing new. I researched for a nudge, and discovered a lot of people sorting by sourcetype="stream:http". That makes sense, we are looking at web traffic to servers. I added in the source IP as the one for the server, and the first result is: poisonivy-is-coming-for-you-batman.jpeg
(My final query was: sourcetype="stream:http" src_ip=192.168.250.70)

