What is the name of the executable uploaded by Po1s0n1vy?
First attempt at analysis on this question was to query:
(src_ip=23.22.63.114 OR src_ip=40.80.148.42) "*exe*"
This showed 2 results by filename: /_vti_bin/shtml.exe and 3791.exe
3791.exe was the correct answer.

What is the MD5 hash of the executable uploaded?
I added the previous answer to the filter (removed the "*exe*" and added filename=3791.exe), but that only returned the previous log and nothing else. No hash values there.
Next, I tried removing that clause entirely and just having: (src_ip=23.22.63.114 OR src_ip=40.80.148.42) "3791.exe", to search for that filename in anything. This did give only 2 results, but neither of them showed a hash of any sort. I then realized I was technically still filtering web traffic only. I wondered if it was possible this filename showed up anywhere else, so I removed the entire src_ip clause, and that returned 76 results. I added in a filter for "MD5", but that was still 67 unique results. I saw that some of the results were coming from sysmon, so I figured I would add that to the filter. I saw filtering on command line commands was an option, so this is the final query I had:
index="botsv1" sysmon CommandLine="3791.exe"
That only returns 1 MD5 hash: AAE3F5A29935E6ABCC2C2754D12A9AF0

